      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Henenlotter's guerrilla filmmaking techniques influenced a generation of DIY horror directors, including early works by <a href=\"/movie/997350\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"997350\">Peter Jackson</a> like <a href=\"/movie/9964\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9964\">Bad Taste</a> (1987) and <a href=\"/movie/8216\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8216\">Meet the Feebles</a> (1989). The film's blend of horror and dark comedy can be seen in modern indies like The Editor (2014) and Psycho Goreman (2020), which similarly embrace practical effects and outlandish premises while maintaining emotional authenticity."
      }
